findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase addressed the from_file_or_default swallowing all errors. The
    config loading tests and implementation don't distinguish NotFound from parse/permission
    errors.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: dev
  evidence: "Reviewer verified: 'CWE-209 \u2014 CliError Display impls don't leak\
    \ internal details (error.rs:14-43)'. Dev implemented sanitized Display. However,\
    \ the reviewer did not flag that eprintln!('error: {e}') still prints Display\
    \ directly to stderr \u2014 the Io(transparent) variant forwards OS details. Partial\
    \ catch by dev, but the stderr leakage path was not fully flagged."
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: "TEA wrote header injection tests for CRLF in tenant values (siem_client.rs:160-189).\
    \ Reviewer also flagged that with_tenant() bypasses validation. However, the specific\
    \ finding about using raw String instead of TenantId from axiathon-core was not\
    \ addressed \u2014 the fix was CRLF validation, not type-safe TenantId usage.\
    \ Partially caught."
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer verified workspace dependency alignment for clap, serde, thiserror,
    uuid, chrono but did not flag that 6 other deps (clap_complete, comfy-table, csv,
    dirs, reqwest, toml) use direct version strings instead of workspace = true.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged as [HIGH]: 'RawConfig silently accepts unknown fields\
    \ \u2014 config typo swallowing at config.rs:11' and recommended adding #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)].\
    \ This covers the token silently ignored scenario."
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in any test. The reviewer did not flag this specific test logic issue.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. Neither TEA nor reviewer flagged this vacuous test.
